<title>GERMANY: Deutsche H1 gp net income up 27.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Deutsche H1 gp net income up 27.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net income			    1,500  vs 1,200</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit			2,800  vs 2,200</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions		     500    vs 800</p>
<p>    Group trading income			2,000  vs 1,400</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 5,700  vs 5,300</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     4,100  vs 3,300</p>
<p>    Group administration costs		8,900  vs 7,000</p>
<p>    Group earnings per share		  2.90 dmk vs 2.30 dmk</p>
<p>    Group taxes				   1,300  vs 1,100</p>
<p>    Group balance sheet total		 996,100 vs 886,100</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Deutsche Bank AG. Earnings compare with first half of 1996, balance sheet total compares with end-1996 level. The bank will hold a news conference at 0800 GMT today to outline its results.</p>
<p>Net income was above analysts' expectations which had averaged 1.36 billion marks, a rise of 16.2 percent. Predictions ranged from 1.28 billion marks to 1.459 billion.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
